--- !u!114 &3406272459873303059
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2191213283747029285}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a78beda5f9f89544aa4b58662bd1aebd, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::LoreMenu
  fillColor: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  autoSubscribe: 1
  tmp: {fileID: 6011429769493505825}
  texts:
  - "So you've come here in search of power, too? Over the years, I\u2019ve seen
    many like you."
  - Listen carefully... I don't have much else to offer besides words. And believe
    me, here... words carry a lot of weight.
  - A long time ago... too long ago for the exact number to matter... they arrived.
    No one knew their origin. No one understood their nature. But their power made
    them indistinguishable from gods.
  - 'Incomprehensible beings who provided humanity with riches, power, and everything
    they could ever want. But never for free.

'
  - They weren't looking for faith or devotion. They wanted absolute control. Every
    decision, action, thought... everything. Humanity didn't live... it obeyed.
  - 'There were many of them. And each one had their own interests.

'
  - 'Some wanted absolute order. A perfect world. Without mistakes. Without freedom.
    Others wanted chaos. Conflict. Destruction.

'
  - "Some needed to be understood\u2026 to be deciphered. As if simply existing weren\u2019t
    enough. Others fed off fear."
  - It all ended in wars. Not between them. Between humanity. Controlled by them,
    of course.
  - "Because they were\u2026 incompatible. They couldn\u2019t coexist. Their very
    nature made it impossible for them to share the same world without destroying
    it."
  - But then something happened that would completely change the course of events...
    writing appeared. And someone... someone understood its power.
  - Words didn't just describe reality. They affected them. Somehow... control passed
    into the hands of humanity. And at that moment... everything began to fall apart.
  - "Entire civilizations rose up against one another. Cults, empires, scholars\u2026
    all trying to control their god\u2026 to destroy the others. Words became weapons.
    Every symbol, every phrase\u2026 could tip the scales."
  - The world barely survived that. But there was... a group. No one remembers their
    names. No one remembers where they came from. But they understood something that
    the others didn't.
  - "Humanity was doomed to self-destruction unless it acted in time. They couldn\u2019t
    drive them out... but they could seal them away."
  - 'They used writing... flawless, without error... rituals that brooked no mistakes...
    and they banished them. All of them. They pushed them out... far away... where
    they couldn''t touch them.

'
  - "And so\u2026 the age of the gods came to an end. Or so the world believed."
  - "Time passed. Everything became myth\u2026 legend\u2026 nonsense meant to scare
    children. And humanity carried on\u2026 blissfully ignorant. Until it arrived\u2026\r\n"
  - 'INTERNET.



'
  - 'A web woven from words... images... repetition... addiction... The perfect place
    for something... to begin seeping in.



'
  - 'They couldn''t go back to the way things were. Not at first. So they did it
    little by little.

'
  - "Memes. Videos. Absurd clips. Things you see... share... and forget. But they
    aren\u2019t random. They never were. Every repetition shapes them. Every time
    something goes viral, something on the other side becomes more real.\n"
  - "And no one sees it. Because these days... nothing on the Internet seems real.
    It\u2019s the best hiding place they\u2019ve ever had.\r\n"
  - 'They already know what happened in the past and what humanity is capable of;
    this time, they won''t make the same mistake.


'
  - 'Old-school Internet users. People who had spent far too long lost in forgotten
    forums, defunct chat rooms, and websites that no one should have been visiting
    anymore.

'
  - They started finding .txt files hidden where they shouldn't be. Strange patterns
    caught our attention. They weren't old files, they were recent ones... and they
    had placed them strategically.
  - "They wanted to return. And now\u2026 they\u2019ve found new believers. \r\n"
  - Just like you.
  - 'Cults. Secret online groups. Each one worships a different deity. Each one convinced
    that it holds the key... the right ritual... the perfect sequence.



'
  - They want to summon them. To obtain those occult powers they promise. And you...
  - You're part of all this.
  - "Every word you write... every mistake... every success... It\u2019s something
    far greater than a simple ritual.\n"
  - 'So tell me... do you really think you''re playing to win? Or are they the ones
    using you to make a comeback?

'
  - But of course... You know how this works, don't you? After all... this is the
    Internet. Anything could be fake here.
  - "But the real question isn\u2019t if this is real or just another viral trend.
    What you should really be asking yourself is...\r\r\n"
  - Why do you keep writing?
  textAppearSpeed: 0.3
  clickAction: {fileID: -8619944142541535279, guid: 052faaac586de48259a63d0c4782560b, type: 3}
  numInteractionsToAnger: 10
  endMessage: ...
  angerMessage: LET ME REST IN PEACE.
